M COMPKEY.C
F RunSearch
S ========================================================================
S Define Section
S ========================================================================
S ========================================================================
S Declarations Section
S ========================================================================
S ========================================================================
S Definitions Section
S ========================================================================
S =========================================================================
S Run the Search Function
D Run the Search Function
R PLU selected or 0 for none

M COMPKEY.C
F InputLine
S =========================================================================
S Input a character string
D Input a character string
P Zero based X co-ordinate (origin Top left)
P Zero based Y co-ordinate (origin Top left)
P The attribute
P The string to start with
P The maximum width of the input string
P The current keyboard cursor x co-ordinate (the flashing cursor)
P The current keyboard cursor y co-ordinate 
P The current keyboard cursor width 
P The current keyboard cursor height 
R The input string

M COMPKEY.C
F TitleBar
S =========================================================================
S Output the Title bar
D Output the Title bar
P The product code i.e. PLU
P The product description
P The 12 character product description for the key top
P Value (price level) 1
P Value (price level) 2
P Value (price level) 3
P Value (price level) 4
P Value (price level) 5
P Value (price level) 6
P TRUE kitchen print == 'Y', FALSE kitchen print == 'N'
P TRUE key is a MENU key, FALSE key is a Single Shot key

M COMPKEY.C
F StatusLine
S =========================================================================
S Output a series of status items in the status box
D Output a series of status items in the status box
P A series of string pairs the first is the key the second the action
P TRUE if the status bar should FLASH

M COMPKEY.C
F KeyInd
S =========================================================================
S Output the key movement indicator
D Output the key movement indicator i.e. show the key number, level and 
D available movement keys
P Zero based X co-ordinate (origin Top left)
P Zero based Y co-ordinate (origin Top left)
P The key number (department)
P Bit flags of available movement keys, bit 4-left 3-right 2-up 1-down 
P The current keyboard level (0-2)

M COMPKEY.C
F SetCurXY
S =========================================================================
S Set the cursor X and Y co-ordinates from the key number
D Set the cursor X and Y co-ordinates from the key number
P The List of keyboard layout information
P The number of keys on the keyboard
P The address of the integer to set to the X co-ordinate
P The address of the integer to set to the Y co-ordinate

M COMPKEY.C
F KeyAtPos
S =========================================================================
S Return TRUE if there is a key at a given X/Y co-ordinate
D Return TRUE if there is a key at a given X/Y co-ordinate
P The List of keyboard layout information
P The number of keys on the keyboard
P The X co-ordinate of the key
P The Y co-ordinate of the key
R TRUE there is a key, FALSE there isn't

M COMPKEY.C
F DrawKey
S =========================================================================
S Draw one key with it's text
D Draw one key with it's text
P The List of keyboard layout information
P The number of keys on the keyboard
P The key index
P The start X co-ordinate of the key
P The start Y co-ordinate of the key
P The keyboard overlay information
P The current keyboard level
P TRUE if the title bar should be draw as well (i.e. the current key)
P The width in characters of the key
P The height in characters of the key
R The available movement key flags (see KeyInd()) if the title is drawn

M COMPKEY.C
F DrawMenu
S =========================================================================
S Draw a menu box on the right hand side
D Draw a menu box on the right hand side
P The current key
P The keyboard overlay information
P The current keyboard level

M COMPKEY.C
F ToggleState
S =========================================================================
S Toggle the state of a key between Menu and Single Shot
D Toggle the state of a key between Menu and Single Shot
P The key to toggle
P The keyboard overlay information

M COMPKEY.C
F KeyGrid
S =========================================================================
S Draw the keyboard grid
D Draw the keyboard grid
P The current key
P The keyboard layout information
P The number of keys
P The start X co-ordinate
P The start Y co-ordinate
P The keyboard overlay information
P The current keyboard level
P The key width in characters
P The key height in characters

M COMPKEY.C
F main
S =========================================================================
S COMPKEY.EXE
D COMPKEY.EXE
R ErrorLevel = 0 on error 1 OK

M FILEIO.C
F CleanBuf
S ========================================================================
S Definitions Section
S ========================================================================
S =========================================================================
S Remove any spaces at the start and end of a string
D Remove any spaces at the start and end of a string
P The padded string
R The cleaned string

M FILEIO.C
F GetLong
S =========================================================================
S Get a LONG from an ASCII string
D Get a LONG from an ASCII string given an offset and length
P The source string
P The offset of the start of the long
P The length of the string containing a long
P The address of the returned long
R TRUE return value OK.  FALSE on error

M FILEIO.C
F GetInt
S =========================================================================
S Get a INT from an ASCII string
D Get a INT from an ASCII string given an offset and length
P The source string
P The offset of the start of the INT
P The length of the string containing a INT
P The address of the returned INT
R TRUE return value OK.  FALSE on error

M FILEIO.C
F GetString
S =========================================================================
S Get a String from an ASCII string
D Get a String from an ASCII string given an offset and length
P The source string
P The offset of the start of the String
P The length of the string containing a String
P The address of the returned String
R TRUE return value OK.  FALSE on error

M FILEIO.C
F LoadDepartment
S =========================================================================
S Load a department file into a linked list
D Load a department file into a linked list
P the file name
P A pointer to the empty linked list i.e. *(deptlist)==NULL
R TRUE if all OK. FALSE if memory or file error. 

M FILEIO.C
F LoadPLU
S =========================================================================
S Load a PLU file into a linked list
D Load a PLU file into a linked list
P the file name
P A pointer to the empty linked list i.e. *(plulist)==NULL
R TRUE if all OK. FALSE if memory or file error. 

M FILEIO.C
F SaveDepartment
S =========================================================================
S Save a department file from a linked list
D Save a department file from a linked list and conditionally
D free the memory associated with the list
P The department file
P The department linked list
P TRUE if the memory associated with the list should be free'd
R TRUE if OK, FALSE on file error or deptlist==NULL or deptlist empty

M FILEIO.C
F SavePLU
S =========================================================================
S Save a PLU file from a linked list
D Save a PLU file from a linked list and conditionally
D free the memory associated with the list
P The PLU file
P The PLU linked list
P TRUE if the memory associated with the list should be free'd
R TRUE if OK, FALSE on file error or plulist==NULL or plulist empty

M FILEIO.C
F LoadKeyDef
S =========================================================================
S Load the keyboard definitions
D Load the keyboard definitions
P file name 
P keyboard overlay
R TRUE on OK, FALSE on ERROR

M FILEIO.C
F LoadLayout
S =========================================================================
S Load a keyboard layout file
D Load a keyboard layout file into an array of ULONGs in the format
D bits 31-24 the line of the key
D bits 23-16 the column of the key
D bits 15-00 the key number (department)
P The keyboard layout file
P The address of an INT for the returned number of keys
P The address of an INT for the returned key width in characters
P The address of an INT for the returned key height in characters
R a pointer to an array of ULONGs allocated from the heap

M FILEIO.C
F main
S =========================================================================
S main used for unit testing of FILEIO.C
D Load PLUFile (argv[1]) Load DeptFile (argv[2])
D list the contents of both on stdout
D Save the PLU Linked list into "PLU.DAT" and free it's memory
D Save the Dept. Linked list into "DEPT.DAT"  and free it's memory
P should be 3
P [0]=command [1]=PLUFile [2]=DeptFile
R ErrLevel = 0,OK 1,Invalid args 2,PLU file error 3,DEPT file error

M VIDEOKBD.C
F RestFont
S =========================================================================
S Restore the VGA text font to default values
D Restore the VGA text font to default values

M VIDEOKBD.C
F LoadFont
S =========================================================================
S Load the VGA font from a local array
D Load the VGA font from a local array
P The local array containing the font information

M VIDEOKBD.C
F GetFont
S =========================================================================
S Return the address of a VGA font mapping
D Return the address of a VGA font mapping
P The font type
R The address of the font mapping

M VIDEOKBD.C
F GetKey
S =========================================================================
S Wait for and return a key from the keyboard
D Wait for and return a key from the keyboard
R The key pressed or if an extended key 0-the key pressed

M VIDEOKBD.C
F KeyCursor
S =========================================================================
S Flash a cursor of inverse video while waiting for a key press
D Flash a cursor of inverse video while waiting for a key press
P The x co-ordinate (Zero based) of the top-left corner
P The y co-ordinate (Zero based) of the top-left corner
P The width in characters of the cursor
P The height in characters of the cursor

M VIDEOKBD.C
F Rectangle
S =========================================================================
S Draw a rectangle
D Draw a rectangle using the character output device
P First X Co-ordinate
P First Y Co-ordinate
P Second X Co-ordinate
P Second Y Co-ordinate
P The attribute of the box characters
P The type of the box characters i.e. 0 = ÚÄ   1 = ÉÍ   2 = Ûß

M VIDEOKBD.C
F OutChXY
S =========================================================================
S Output a character of a given colour at an X/Y co-ordinate
D Output a character of a given colour at an X/Y co-ordinate.  
D NOTE: This function has no bounds checking and should not 
D be called directly.  Use OutChar() to perform this function.
P The X co-ordinate (Zero based - origin top left)
P The Y co-ordinate (Zero based - origin top left)
P The attribute
P The character

M VIDEOKBD.C
F OutChar
S =========================================================================
S Output a character on the console
D Output a character on the console at a given x and y co-ordinate.
D Any character that falls outside the clipping viewport will be ignored.
D use SetViewPort() to assign the clipping values.
P Zero based X Co-ordinate (origin Top Left)
P Zero based Y Co-ordinate (origin Top Left)
P The character to output

M VIDEOKBD.C
F OutFormat
S =========================================================================
S Formatted String Output on the console
D Formatted String Output on the console at a given x and y co-ordinate
D using the same formatting commands as printf().
D Any character that falls outside the clipping viewport will be ignored.
D use SetViewPort() to assign the clipping values.
P Zero based X Co-ordinate (origin Top Left)
P Zero based Y Co-ordinate (origin Top Left)
P The attribute
P The format string. NOTE: must NOT result in string length > MAXSTRLEN
P variable parameters

M VIDEOKBD.C
F SetViewPort
S =========================================================================
S Set the View Port clipping parameters
D Set the View Port clipping parameters.
D All subsequent video output will be clipped to these boundaries.
P The minimum X co-ordinated
P The minimum Y co-ordinated
P The maximum X co-ordinated
P The maximum Y co-ordinated
P Zero to leave, The attribute to clear the area covered by the view port

M VIDEOKBD.C
F OutCentre
S =========================================================================
S Output a formatted string centred about an X/Y co-ordinate
D Output a formatted string centred about an X/Y co-ordinate
P Zero based X Co-ordinate (origin Top Left)
P Zero based Y Co-ordinate (origin Top Left)
P The attribute
P The format string. NOTE: must NOT result in string length > MAXSTRLEN
P variable parameters

M VIDEOKBD.C
F OutWrap
S =========================================================================
S Output a string with word wrap, centred.
D Output a string with word wrap, centred.
P Zero based X Co-ordinate (origin Top Left)
P Zero based Y Co-ordinate (origin Top Left)
P The maximum width of any line
P The height (i.e. number of lines)
P The attribute
P The string
R The actual height (i.e. number of lines) of the output string

